<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n49584" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">typus</span></b> , i, m.,
		= <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τύπος</span>. <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<i>A figure</i>, <i>image</i>, on a
			wall, <i><span class="en">Cic. Att. 1, 10, 3</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Plin. 35,
				12, 43, § 151</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Lampr.
				Heliog. 3</span></i> and 7.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b> In medic. lang., <i>a form</i>, <i>type</i>, <i>character</i> of
			intermittent fevers, <i><span class="en">Cael.
				Aur. Acut. 1, 14, 108</span></i>;
				<i><span class="en">App. Herb. 102</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
